{"id":"NCT05550298","title":"Multi-Center Molecular Diagnosis and Host Response of Respiratory Viral Infections in Pediatric Transplant Recipients","official":"Multi-Center Molecular Diagnosis and Host Response of Respiratory Viral Infections in Pediatric Transplant Recipients","summary":"The participants are being asked to take part in this clinical trial, a type of research study, because the participants are scheduled to receive or have recently received a hematopoietic cell transplant (HCT) or a solid organ transplant (SOT).\n\nPrimary Objective\n\nTo determine if pre-transplant screening for respiratory viral load predicts RVI within 1- year post-transplant among survivors.\n\nSecondary Objectives:\n\n* To develop and validate a classifier based on pre-transplant immunological profile predictive of developing an acute respiratory viral infection (aRVI), with RSV/PIV3/HMPV/SARS-CoV-2 through one-year post-transplant among survivors.\n* To develop and validate a classifier based on Day +100 post-transplant immunological profiles predictive of developing an acute respiratory viral infection (aRVI),with RSV/PIV3/HMPV/SARS-CoV-2 through one-year post-transplant among survivors .","conditions":["Hematopoietic Cell Transplant","Solid Organ Transplant","Respiratory Viral Infection"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Recipient Inclusion Criteria\n\n* Less than 18 years at the time of anticipated transplant\n* Participant meets one of the following criteria:\n\n  1. scheduled to receive allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplant within 14 days of enrollment or\n  2. Scheduled to or received solid organ transplant within 7 days before or after enrollment\n* Participant is receiving care at the time of enrollment at one of the study participating institutions.\n* Parent/guardian willing and able to provide informed consent, and if appropriate, child willing and able to provide informed assent.\n\nDonor Inclusion Criteria\n\n* Donor for HCT recipient enrolled on the VIPER study.\n* Willing and able to provide informed consent.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\nRecipient Exclusion Criteria\n\nNone\n\nDonor Exclusion Criteria\n\n* Is not an HCT donor for a participant enrolled on the VIPER study.\n* Not available to provide pre-transplant research blood sample.","minAge":"","maxAge":"18 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":2000,"start":"2022-12-13","pcd":"2027-08","upd":"2025-10-02","sponsor":"Arkansas Children's Hospital Research Institute","areas":["other"],"central":["Gabriela Maron, MD · 866-278-5833 · referralinfo@stjude.org","William J. Steinbach, MD · 501-364-5262 · wsteinbach@uams.edu"],"sites":[{"f":"University of Alabama at Birmingham's (UAB)","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35294","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Maria Rueda Altez, MD · 205-638-2599 · mruedaaltez@uabmc.edu"},{"f":"Arkansas Children's Hospital","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72202","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"William J. Steinbach, MD · 501-364-5262 · wsteinbach@uams.edu"},{"f":"Children's National Medical","city":"Washington D.C.","pr":"District of Columbia","zip":"20010","s":"R","lat":38.8951,"lon":-77.0364,"c":"Benjamin Hanisch, MD · 202-476-5051 · Bhanisch@childrensnational.org"},{"f":"University if Miami","city":"Miami","pr":"Florida","zip":"33146","s":"R","lat":25.7743,"lon":-80.1937,"c":"Ivan Gonzalez, MD · i.gonzalez2@med.miami.edu"},{"f":"Emory and Children's Healthcare of Atlanta","city":"Atlanta","pr":"Georgia","zip":"30322","s":"R","lat":33.749,"lon":-84.388,"c":"Kathryn Goggin, MD · 404-785-5437 · kathryn.pearl.goggin@emory.edu"},{"f":"University of Chicago Medicine Comer Children's Hospital","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60637","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Madan Kumar, MD · 773-702-7087 · mkumar@peds.bsd.uchicago.edu"},{"f":"University of Louisville","city":"Louisville","pr":"Kentucky","zip":"40202","s":"R","lat":38.2542,"lon":-85.7594,"c":"Vict